(## Serving hyperparameters and calibration) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The original 24 workloads are retained: batch 1/4/8, prompt 32/128/512/896, output 32/64. Attention) Tj
T*
(candidates are eager off and the eight custom tile/warp combinations BM 16/32, BN 32/64, warps 4/8. KV-) Tj
T*
(cache candidates are off, dynamic, static request-sized capacity, and static full-context capacity.) Tj
T*
(Request capacity is prompt + output - 1, matching actual stored positions. The isolated cache extension) Tj
T*
(affects only this new frozen runner; old studies remain untouched.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Per training configuration and workload, calibrate every attention/cache setting on seed 42, with two) Tj
T*
(warmups and three measured repetitions. Independently best/poor attention comes from custom tiles with) Tj
T*
(cache off; independently best/poor cache comes from policies with eager attention. Joint extrema select) Tj
T*
(the paired custom-attention/cache combination. Selection is latency-based among passing cells, with) Tj
T*
(memory retained as a separate objective. There is no universal scalar optimum across quality, latency and) Tj
T*
(memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Freeze selections before confirmation. The 27 independently selected states and four joint states run on) Tj
T*
(all three model seeds using a separate prompt stream, two warmups and seven measured repetitions. Case) Tj
T*
(order is randomized reproducibly. This provides 2,592 calibration and 2,232 confirmation cells per) Tj
T*
(task/precision. Labels may coincide where there is only one eligible candidate; this is explicitly) Tj
T*
(recorded and is not an invented tuning gain.) Tj
